            "text": "{\"claims\":[{\"type\":\"wrong_strength\",\"location\":\"IsLinearMap ℝ (λ x ↦ f i x + fderiv ℝ g x (Pi.single i 1))\",\"explanation\":\"The informal problem explicitly allows a constant term in each “linear” function, while `IsLinearMap` requires a genuinely linear function. This may not change the existential theorem: a suitable change to g might absorb the constant terms.\",\"prediction\":\"The comparison may be provable despite the difference in the property required of a particular g. If so, this is a wording mismatch rather than a defect in the theorem.\",\"probe_kind\":\"equivalence\",\"comparison\":\"(∀ (n : ℕ) (hn : 1 ≤ n) (f : Fin n → ((Fin n → ℝ) → ℝ)) (hf : ∀ i, ContDiff ℝ 2 (f i)) (C : Fin n → Fin n → ℝ) (hf' : ∀ i j : Fin n, ∀ x : Fin n → ℝ, fderiv ℝ (f i) x (Pi.single j 1) - fderiv ℝ (f j) x (Pi.single i 1) = C i j), ∃ g : (Fin n → ℝ) → ℝ, ∀ i : Fin n, IsLinearMap ℝ (fun x => f i x + fderiv ℝ g x (Pi.single i 1))) ↔ (∀ (n : ℕ) (hn : 1 ≤ n) (f : Fin n → ((Fin n → ℝ) → ℝ)) (hf : ∀ i, ContDiff ℝ 2 (f i)) (C : Fin n → Fin n → ℝ) (hf' : ∀ i j : Fin n, ∀ x : Fin n → ℝ, fderiv ℝ (f i) x (Pi.single j 1) - fderiv ℝ (f j) x (Pi.single i 1) = C i j), ∃ g : (Fin n → ℝ) → ℝ, ∀ i : Fin n, ∃ (a₀ : ℝ) (a : Fin n → ℝ), ∀ x : Fin n → ℝ, f i x + fderiv ℝ g x (Pi.single i 1) = a₀ + ∑ j : Fin n, a j * x j)\",\"witnesses\":null,\"edit_from\":null,\"edit_to\":null,\"bridge\":\"translated\",\"obligation\":\"Review the affine-form comparison against the informal definition, and determine whether the existential choice of g makes the two full propositions equivalent. A difference between the predicates for a fixed g alone would not establish a defect.\"}],\"summary\":\"The conclusion uses strict linearity where the informal definition permits affine functions; whether this changes the existential claim remains to be tested.\"}"
